+What: /dev/a081-nordic
+Date: October 2026
+Contact: Qiyu Project <qiyu@example.invalid>
+Description:
+        Exclusive, root-only access to the A081 Nordic radio transport.
+        poll() reports readable after a data-ready IRQ. Use a bounded poll
+        timeout in userspace; the driver does not wait for a radio IRQ inside
+        the ioctl. A081_NORDIC_IOC_TRANSFER from linux/a081-nordic.h exchanges
+        exactly 36 bytes, SPI mode 0, 8 bits per word, at the DT clock rate.
+        With no unconsumed IRQ it returns EAGAIN; removal returns ENODEV/HUP.
+
+        Only tx[36] is input. Output includes raw rx[36], CLOCK_MONOTONIC
+        data-ready IRQ and transfer-completion times in ns, and a cumulative
+        IRQ sequence. Sequence gaps expose coalesced notifications, not a
+        claim about the number of buffered radio packets. An IRQ during an
+        exchange remains pending. Timestamp fields are host transport times,
+        not controller IMU sampling/exposure times. One old notification may
+        be visible on reopening; inspect returned RX and sequence.
+
+        No framing/CRC, retry, pairing, haptic, or controller-clock policy is
+        implemented in the kernel. The observed OEM idle TX is 36 bytes of
+        0xee; valid RX begins a5 5a. Userspace must decode packets and retain
+        queued commands until the protocol acknowledges them. A transfer can
+        consume a packet even if copying its result to userspace fails.
+
+What: /sys/bus/spi/devices/spiB.C/irq_count
+What: /sys/bus/spi/devices/spiB.C/transfer_count
+Date: October 2026
+Contact: Qiyu Project <qiyu@example.invalid>
+Description:
+        Data-ready interrupts and successful SPI exchanges since probe.
+        These count transport activity, not valid controller packets.
